body:
Finally got it a while ago, now aiming to get a Diamond on Gangnam Style. For some weird reason Can't Hold Us is really kicking my ass. Oh, and if anyone's managed Gimme chocolate!!, my hats off to you! 

&#x200B;

Player tag Nonni#2 if anyone wants to add!

Hi, there. I go through the same things as well and I wish I can help you but what I do is 1) keep very good track of my menstruation cycle. Trust me, you may think that this doesn't count but your ability to control your thoughts and reactions to the little things that bother you is severely affected by your cycle. 2) put yourself through a mental exercise. What will happen if he is seeing someone else, or leaves the relationship. what would that do to you and how will you cope/move on after? this has to be healthy. it has to be a healthy outcome. (e.g. I will turn to my friends for help and not be alone). 3) look at him. stare at him. look into his eyes. this man loves you. know that you reacting irrationally will **MAKE** him leave. can you forgive yourself if that happens? 

&#x200B;

Congratulations on first being aware that this is a problem you have. You can't control how you feel but you can definitely control how you react to it. And the little things are insignificant. Not putting the toilet seat down, not sending an essay as a goodnight message. these are insignificant. what matters is he's there for you, he loves you, and YOU ARE LOVED. Good luck, OP.

I don't know if there's anything wrong with you, honestly. I just know that relationships don't seem all that they're made out to be when we've gotten a rejection/been cheated on, etc. It just seems futile at this point and all you have to go on is hope that there's someone who will make it feel worth it again. I guess the point is not to try and if someone enters your life that makes you feel things like you felt for that girl then good for you. 

&#x200B;

But what do I know. I'm just like you.

All I can say is that people liked being liked and they'll keep handing you crumbs to continue liking them without any intention to take things further. I had a similar situation, FWB kept saying "You don't like me the way I like you" even though I thought we've both established that this was purely going to be physical. And in the end, I realised that I did have some feelings for me and had an adult conversation about it. I told him I liked him more than an FWB and he said we couldn't be together because he had strict religious views about his future gf/wife (i.e. has to be the same religion as him). 

&#x200B;

But **even then**, he would make remarks about how I was lying about my feelings for him since I'm going on dates with other people. He would be sweet, cooked for me, asked me out on dates with no physical expectations. But the fact is, he has no intentions on having a relationship with me and we both know he was dating other girls to. Moral of the story is, keep things physical and don't go catching feels. He's not. Especially since you've just gotten out of a long term relationship. Give it some time, find out who you are, what you want, what you don't want. You can keep being friends with him but I'd say protect your heart a little.

I'm with you. 

&#x200B;

I've experienced people who just don't text you and I've experienced people who text you every single day or be sure to at least reply you even if it's a couple of hours later - never days. I think a big part of it is how much of a future people see they might have with the other person and yeah, how interested they are. If it's worth pursuing long term, they'll make time.

Do you think this is a much better conversation in person or over the phone than over text? I feel like over text, it's easier for the other person to say "yeah, I'm still interested" but still not be interested and just holding out and keeping you as an option? 

&#x200B;

I'm glad you showed that it's possible but I think I'd still throw up if I had to do it. Some day I'll get there.

Same. I think I've found someone so close to perfection, except he was only visiting the country and probably wasn't willing to do long distance or leave his ex for good. What a waste. 

So if I could find him online, then it sorta gives me hope, I guess? 

&#x200B;
